From 592b81d23adb913f919a4c0dfafae7ff61fe4793 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 10:16:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Kanban: hold a card whose profile owner's service is
 failed instead of booking crashes

A failed/masked/disabled gateway service is a persistent owner-down state, not a crash.
The worker exits KANBAN_OWNER_DOWN_EXIT_CODE (68) for it before admission; the sweep books
owner_down and requeues uncounted (same admission/streak limits as owner_unavailable). Before
claiming for a non-default profile the dispatcher runs the read-only systemd probe; on a
persistent code it claims nothing, parks the card scheduled (owner_down:<profile>:<code>) with a
wake check on the unit state, and files one deduped 'profile <p> owner down: <code>' card under
the open card that works on the unit (later holds comment on it).

example gateway 2026-11-02: example-card (askeve-builder, unit failed) was booked crashed twice
in 40 s and sent to triage with no turn run (self-heal defect kanban-ef16a9e091).
